# Vulnerabilities the eval gates accept on purpose: `make scan-deps` and the image gate,
# `make scan-image-<family>` / `scan-image-cpu-<family>`, which publish-image-* runs.
# trivy reads this file as --ignorefile.
#
# One advisory id per line; `#` starts a comment. Every alias of an advisory is listed
# (CVE, GHSA, PYSEC), because trivy reports by CVE or, when an advisory has none, by
# GHSA, while osv-scanner and quay's scanner name the same advisory by GHSA or PYSEC.
# The aliases were taken from the advisory records at osv.dev; do not derive one id
# from another. Each id carries trivy's expiry, exp:YYYY-MM-DD: past that date the line
# no longer applies and the gate fails again, so the entry is re-reviewed (until
# 2027-05-31 unless the entry says otherwise). Every entry names the images it
# applies to, why the finding is accepted, and the issue that removes it; delete the
# entry when that lands.
#
# One file serves every family, and trivy matches ids alone: an id accepted here is
# accepted in every image. Each entry is scoped by package and version in its comment,
# so a new finding with a listed id in another package or image is not covered by it
# and needs an entry (or a fix) of its own.

